    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (72.21) serving as our undisputed anchor, buoyed by an favorable matchup against King, M and his 4.39 xERA. While **Kyle Tucker** is the clear start, the most aggressive play on the board is **Drake Baldwin** (70.07). The combination of a soft matchup against Williamson (5.64 xERA) and the elevated production expected from the #2 hole makes **Drake Baldwin** a high-leverage start to capitalize on early-inning run production. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** (62.40) provides excellent value in the leadoff spot; his 0.381 xwOBA against Lynch IV suggests that his high score is well-supported by underlying plate discipline and situational upside.\n\nEfficiency remains the priority, which forced a difficult benching decision for **Brayan Rocchio** (38.00). Despite a favorable park factor, **Brayan Rocchio** was sidelined by a combination of a tough opponent in Tolle and an optimizer threshold that strictly enforces a 40.0 floor to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, we are navigating the fallout of the **Gunnar Henderson** rainout, which effectively removed our primary offensive engine from the day\u2019s ledger. While we remain thin due to the ongoing IL stints of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, the presence of **Jackson Merrill** (58.27) provides a critical hedge; his ability to exploit a slow delivery from Stewart gives him an edge in the stolen base department, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on the lower half of our lineup, specifically **Wade Meckler** (40.85) and **Liam Hicks** (43.04). Both hover near the \"Marginal\" threshold, with **Liam Hicks** specifically suffering from a negative platoon split against Rod\u00f3n. We are banking on the high-floor production of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.65) and **Josh Jung** (51.17) to stabilize the middle of the order, provided they can overcome the SP skill of Rasmussen and Manaea, respectively. With the roster currently depleted of stars like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and depth pieces like **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Tommy White**, and **Henry Bolte**, today\u2019s performance rests squarely on the shoulders of our top-tier outfield and the reliability of **Miguel Vargas** at the top.",
